 "speed": 0.9,
 "text": "Why do AI products stall after the demo? Usually, nobody can measure whether a change made things better. And fixing one prompt breaks another. Hamel Husain's answer is three levels of evals. Level one: unit tests. Cheap checks that run on every change, like making sure no raw IDs leak into a reply. Level two: log your traces, and have people review them, marking each one simply good or bad. Then build an AI judge, and check that it agrees with them. To make that easy, build a simple viewer for your own data. Show the scenario, the output, and one click to label it. Level three is A/B testing, once the product is mature. But the real lesson is simpler. Look at your data, again and again. That is how you move fast.",
